  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{cos}^{2}\u2061t={sin}^{2}\u2061t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061t-1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061t{tan}^{2}\u2061t} & =\\frac{-1\\cdot (1-{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta )}{{cos}^{2}\u2061t{tan}^{2}\u2061t} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}\u2061t}{{cos}^{2}\u2061t\\cdot {tan}^{2}\u2061t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the denominator using the definition of $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta $ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{sin}^{2}\u2061t}{{cos}^{2}\u2061t\\cdot {tan}^{2}\u2061t} & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}\u2061t}{{cos}^{2}\u2061t\\cdot {(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}\u2061t}{{cos}^{2}\u2061t\\cdot (\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061t}{{cos}^{2}\u2061t})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}\u2061t}{(\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061t\\cdot {sin}^{2}\u2061t}{{cos}^{2}\u2061t})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}\u2061t}{(\\frac{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}\u2061t}\\cdot {sin}^{2}\u2061t}{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}\u2061t}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{sin}^{2}\u2061t}{{sin}^{2}\u2061t} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\cancel{{sin}^{2}\u2061t}}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}\u2061t}} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061t-1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061t{tan}^{2}\u2061t}=-1\n$$",
